o position to the right of position 2. Thus, this possibility is invalid.\n\n#### Possibility 2: Videographer in position 1 and pakistani in position 2\n- Position 1: videographer\n- Position 2: pakistani\nCheck the second constraint: \"videographer is somewhere to the left of the person who watches animation.\"\nThis means the animation-watcher must be to the right of position 1. Hence, position 2 watches animation.\n\n### Step 5: Fill in other attributes\n- **Positions**:\n  - Position 1: videographer\n  - Position 2: pakistani\n\n- **Nationalities**: pakistani is in position 2, so position 1 must be nigerian (since nationalities are unique).\n- **Jobs**: videographer is in position 1, so position 2 must be freelancer (since jobs are unique).\n- **Movie-Genres**:\n  - Position 2 watches animation (from the constraint).\n  - Thus, position 1 watches thriller (since movie genres are unique).\n\n### Step 6: Verify uniqueness\n- Jobs: videographer (position 1), freelancer (position 2) - unique.\n- Movie-Genres: thriller (position 1), animation (position 2) - unique.\n- Nationalities: nigerian (position 1), pakistani (position 2) - unique.\n\n### Step 7: Answer the questions\n1. **What is the job of the person who is pakistani?**\n   The pakistani is in position 2, who is a freelancer.\n\n2. **What is the movie genre of the person who is pakistani?**\n   The pakistani is in position 2, who watches animation.\n\n3. **What movie genre does the person in position 1 watch?**\n   The person in position 1 watches thriller.\n\n4. **At what position is the person who is a videographer?**\n   The videographer is in position 1.\n\n### Final answers:\n<solution>freelancer, animation, thriller, 1</solution>\n\nFinal answer: <solution>freelancer, animation, thriller, 1</solution>", "logprobs": [{"token": "Let", "logprob": -0.2458193153142929}, {"token": "'s", "logprob": -0.027289140969514847}, {"token": " analyze", "logprob": -0.5875506401062012}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.02